<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Suppress SQLitePCLRaw version-specific RID warning (third-party library issue) -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NETSDK1206</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Transitive-package CVE overrides.

    The GitHub Actions Dependency Review job fails any PR whose dependency graph
    contains a moderate-or-higher CVE. Older Avalonia 11.0.2 + LiveCharts 2.0.0-rc1
    pull in transitive packages that have published advisories:

      System.Text.Json     6.0.3       High      GHSA-8g4q-xg66-9fp4
      System.Drawing.Common 4.7.0      Critical  GHSA-rxg9-xrhp-64gj
      SkiaSharp            2.88.3/.5   High      GHSA-j7hp-h8jx-5ppr
      Tmds.DBus.Protocol   0.15.0      High      GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9

    Adding direct PackageReference entries here overrides the transitive
    resolution for every project that inherits this file. NuGet picks the highest
    compatible version that satisfies the constraints from the existing transitive
    graph; the versions below are the patched releases that close each advisory
    while staying within the same major line so Avalonia 11.0.2 and LiveCharts
    2.0.0-rc1 don't need to be bumped at the same time.

    If a future Avalonia / LiveCharts bump moves to newer SkiaSharp etc., these
    overrides can be revisited (or removed if the transitive resolves to a safe
    version on its own).

    PrivateAssets="all" is intentionally NOT set — these overrides must flow
    through to consuming projects via project references; otherwise the
    overrides would only protect the project that declares them.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" Version="2.88.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus.Protocol" Version="0.93.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
